From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 21:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: exynos-acpm: Add Exynos9820

The protocol itself needs nothing new: the message layout, the field
positions and the sequence numbering are the same.  What differs is where
in the shared memory the firmware keeps its channel configuration, and that
is one number.

Read from the vendor device tree of a Galaxy S10+, whose ACPM node states
initdata-base = <0x7000> against the 0xa000 of the SoC this driver was
written for.  Confirmed on the phone: with this offset the driver reads the
configuration, finds eleven channels of the expected shape, and the
firmware answers the doorbell.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c b/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c
index 942a2e9f02f..5a47f12fc16 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@
 #define ACPM_TX_TIMEOUT_US		500000
 
 #define ACPM_GS101_INITDATA_BASE	0xa000
+#define ACPM_EXYNOS9820_INITDATA_BASE	0x7000
 
 /**
  * struct acpm_shmem - shared memory configuration information.
@@ -881,10 +882,18 @@ static const struct acpm_match_data acpm_gs101 = {
 	.acpm_clk_dev_name = "gs101-acpm-clk",
 };
 
+static const struct acpm_match_data acpm_exynos9820 = {
+	.initdata_base = ACPM_EXYNOS9820_INITDATA_BASE,
+	.acpm_clk_dev_name = "exynos9820-acpm-clk",
+};
+
 static const struct of_device_id acpm_match[] = {
 	{
 		.compatible = "google,gs101-acpm-ipc",
 		.data = &acpm_gs101,
+	}, {
+		.compatible = "samsung,exynos9820-acpm-ipc",
+		.data = &acpm_exynos9820,
 	},
 	{},
 };
